# `GROUP BY` after the table, without `|`: pipe into `summarize ... by` (DS0153).
mode: syntax
---- query
from t GROUP BY a
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..18
  PIPELINE@0..17
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "t"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    ERROR@7..17
      IDENT@7..12 "GROUP"
      WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
      IDENT@13..15 "BY"
      WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
      IDENT@16..17 "a"
  WHITESPACE@17..18 "\n"

error[DS0153]: `GROUP BY` is SQL: DataScript pipes the table into an operator
  --> query:1:8
  |
1 | from t GROUP BY a
  |        ^^^^^^^^ expected `|` before this
  |
  = help: group with `summarize ... by` after a `|`: `| summarize count() by a`
